# s8_convert_release (off-path)
#
# basis      s7_graph_clear_values peak 2061808 kB; fourth attempt on its largest object. Single pool.
# object     heap:_multiarray_umath...+0x13ab14, 865.8 MB (41.0%): plaintext weights held twice during
#            ONNX-to-CrypTen conversion (all three s7 replicates peak there). probe_convert_trace_cpu.py:
#            torch_bytes 433258512 -> 866505752 across the initializer loop, RSS follows; _to_crypten
#            (nn/onnx_converter.py:183) builds one tensor per initializer while the HF model is alive.
# earlier
#   off-path/s8_plaintext_free_early   release the caller's copy before the parse
#                                      object 865.8 -> 433.5 MB, peak -0.06% against a 1.364% spread
#   off-path/s8_encrypt_on_convert     also encrypt each initializer as it is created, so the graph's
#                                      copies never accumulate
#                                      object gone from the table entirely, peak -0.47% against 1.41%
#            object removed, peak unchanged: glibc reuses freed pages within the phase.
# fix        as s4_param_mmap_release, window = from_onnx:
#            1. encrypt each initializer in its creating loop (upstream Module.encrypt)
#            2. mallopt(M_MMAP_THRESHOLD, 131072) for from_onnx, restored to 33554432, then malloc_trim(0)
# draws      same crypten.cryptensor calls, tensors and order (insertion = initializer order); part 2
#            consults no generator.
#
# pool_attacked: host
# object_attacked: _multiarray_umath.cpython-310-x86_64-linux-gnu.so+0x13ab14
OMP_NUM_THREADS=8
SHAFT_LEVERS=plaintext_free_early_cpu,triple_share_free_cpu,beaver_reveal_inplace_cpu,graph_clear_values_cpu,param_mmap_release_cpu,onnx_single_file_export_cpu,trace_nograd_cpu,convert_release_cpu
